---
interface Props {
  data: {
    name: string;
    site?: string;
    version: string;
  };
}
const { data } = Astro.props;
const site = data.site ?? 'https://traverse.quest';
---

<div class="ps-page ps-display tv-page">
  <nav class="ps-subnav" aria-label="Traverse sections">
    <a href={site} class="ps-brand" aria-label="Traverse home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <strong>Traverse</strong>
    </a>
    <span class="ps-subnav-links">
      <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
      <a href="#setup">Setup</a>
      <a href="#destinations">Destinations</a>
      <a href="#support">Support</a>
      <a href={site} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit site</a>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <section id="top" class="ps-hero tv-hero" aria-labelledby="traverse-title">
    <div class="ps-hero-copy">
      <p class="ps-eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Travel eSIMs &middot; traverse.quest</p>
      <h1 id="traverse-title">Keep your number. <em>Skip the roaming bill.</em></h1>
      <p class="ps-lede">
        Your carrier charges <span class="tv-nowrap">$10&ndash;15</span> for every day you use data
        abroad. Traverse is one price for the whole trip: choose where you're going, choose how
        much data you need, and set it up before you fly.
      </p>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={site} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find your eSIM</a>
        <a class="ps-btn" href={`${site}/help/phone`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check my phone</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-release-note">
        Data only &middot; no subscription, no daily fees &middot; your home number keeps working on phones that support two lines.
        <a class="tv-note-link" href={`${site}/setup`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the setup guide</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tv-hero-capture">
      <figure class="tv-shot-frame">
        <img
          src="/products/traverse/storefront.png"
          alt="Traverse storefront: a destination form with trip length and data amount, beside an interactive globe of selectable countries."
          width="2880"
          height="1800"
          decoding="async"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <span>01</span> Where, how long, how much data. One price for the trip.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="pricing" class="ps-section tv-pricing" aria-labelledby="tv-pricing-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">01 / Pricing</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="tv-pricing-title">A week abroad, <em>two ways.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        A carrier day pass charges you for every day you use data, whether it's a lot or a little.
        With Traverse you pay once, for the whole trip.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tv-compare">
      <article class="tv-compare-card">
        <p class="ps-index">Carrier pass</p>
        <strong class="tv-compare-price">$70&ndash;105</strong>
        <p class="tv-compare-note">7 days at $10&ndash;15 a day &mdash; and you're charged for any day you use data at all.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="tv-compare-card tv-compare-win">
        <p class="ps-index">Traverse eSIM</p>
        <strong class="tv-compare-price">One price</strong>
        <p class="tv-compare-note">For the whole trip. Single-country plans start at a few dollars, with regional and worldwide plans for when you cross borders.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="tv-plans">
      <div class="tv-plan">
        <h3>Fixed data</h3>
        <p>From 1 GB to 100 GB to use across your trip. The best value when you know how long you're away and roughly how much you'll use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tv-plan">
        <h3>Daily</h3>
        <p>Not sure how much you'll need? Pay only for the days you use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tv-plan">
        <h3>Regional &amp; global</h3>
        <p>One plan for Europe (35 countries) or the whole world (117 countries), so a multi-stop trip needs just one eSIM. Add extra countries when you need them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="setup" class="ps-section tv-setup" aria-labelledby="tv-setup-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">02 / Setup</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="tv-setup-title">Set up in minutes, <em>with pictures.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Five simple steps, each shown on a phone screen, including the settings that stop your
        carrier from charging you. Most plans only start when you first connect abroad, so
        installing early costs nothing.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tv-setup-grid">
      <figure class="tv-setup-shot">
        <img
          src="/products/traverse/setup-guide.png"
          alt="Traverse setup guide showing step one: tap Add eSIM in Settings, with an annotated phone screenshot."
          width="2880"
          height="2000"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <span>02</span> Five steps, each shown on a phone screen.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="tv-steps">
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Check your phone.</strong> It needs to be unlocked and able to use an eSIM. In Settings, Carrier Lock should say <em>No SIM restrictions</em>. It takes about 30 seconds.</li>
          <li><strong>Pick a plan.</strong> Where you're going, for how long, and roughly how much data.</li>
          <li><strong>Pay once.</strong> No subscription, no daily fee. Your QR code and install link show up on your order page and in your email.</li>
          <li><strong>Install.</strong> Open Settings &rarr; Cellular &rarr; Add eSIM while you're on Wi-Fi, at home or at the gate.</li>
          <li><strong>Go.</strong> When you land, turn off roaming on your home line so your carrier can't charge you for data.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="tv-caveat">
          Good to know: some plans can only be installed once, so don't delete the eSIM after
          setting it up. Traverse is data only &mdash; regular calls and texts still go through
          your home line, at your carrier's rates.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="destinations" class="ps-section tv-dest" aria-labelledby="tv-dest-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">03 / Destinations</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="tv-dest-title">Pick a country. <em>See the price.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Every destination has its own page with today's plans, the local networks you'll connect
        to, and the price for the trip length you choose.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="tv-dest-shot">
      <img
        src="/products/traverse/destination-italy.png"
        alt="Traverse Italy page listing fixed-data plans from 1 GB to 100 GB with prices, TIM/Iliad/Wind networks, and a suggested 5 GB plan."
        width="2880"
        height="2000"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span>03</span> Italy: plans, networks and multi-country options on one page.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="why" class="ps-section tv-how" aria-labelledby="tv-how-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">04 / Peace of mind</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="tv-how-title">No surprises <em>at checkout.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Buying data for a trip should be the easy part. Here's what you can count on every time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ps-feature-grid tv-feature-grid">
      <article class="ps-card">
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>The price you see</h3>
        <p>Your quote is held for 15 minutes, so the price you approve is the price you pay.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ps-card">
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Safe, simple payment</h3>
        <p>Pay by card or wallet through Stripe, with no account to create. Your eSIM is only issued once your payment is confirmed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ps-card">
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Up-to-date plans</h3>
        <p>Plans and prices are refreshed throughout the day. If something isn't available, we say so instead of swapping in something else.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ps-card">
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Help when you need it</h3>
        <p>Share or gift an eSIM, top up when you run low, and ask for a refund if plans change. Get help from the built-in assistant, WhatsApp or email.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="support" class="ps-section tv-support" aria-labelledby="tv-support-title">
    <div class="tv-support-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="ps-index">05 / Support</p>
        <h2 id="tv-support-title">Need help with <em>your eSIM?</em></h2>
        <p>
          Get help right on the site. Have your order number handy and we'll pick up where you
          left off. Trouble connecting? There's a quick form just for that.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={`${site}/support`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Support</a>
        <a class="ps-btn" href={`${site}/refunds`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Refunds</a>
        <a class="ps-btn ps-ghost" href="mailto:info@traverse.quest">info@traverse.quest</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
